Register the Thai (th-TH) locale

Appends th-TH to supportedLocales — the array that drives the language picker —
and wires it into the video-export cover resources so an exported MP4 carries
the Thai CTA strings instead of falling back to another language.

Appended at the END of supportedLocales, never inserted mid-array: the first
locale for a language prefix is used as the default when a browser sends a bare
code, so reordering would change behaviour for existing languages. That rule is
OpenMAIC's own (lib/i18n/TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md).

The locale file itself (lib/i18n/locales/th-TH.json) is generated by
deploy/openmaic-patches/build_th_locale.py and copied in separately: adding a
new file needs no patch and can never conflict on rebase.

diff --git a/lib/i18n/locales.ts b/lib/i18n/locales.ts
index cafdbf9d..05ecb2ec 100644
--- a/lib/i18n/locales.ts
+++ b/lib/i18n/locales.ts
@@ -26,4 +26,5 @@ export const supportedLocales = [
   { code: 'fr-FR', label: 'Français', shortLabel: 'FR' },
   { code: 'vi-VN', label: 'Tiếng Việt', shortLabel: 'VI' },
   { code: 'de-DE', label: 'Deutsch', shortLabel: 'DE' },
+  { code: 'th-TH', label: 'ไทย', shortLabel: 'TH' },
 ] as const satisfies readonly LocaleEntry[];
diff --git a/lib/video-export-app/cover-config.ts b/lib/video-export-app/cover-config.ts
index 279fcaf5..c1af2fd9 100644
--- a/lib/video-export-app/cover-config.ts
